<h1>Prompt Engineering Basics</h1>

<p>
Prompt engineering is the practice of crafting effective inputs for AI models to generate useful outputs. Good prompts help the AI understand your intention and deliver accurate, relevant results.
</p>

<h2>What is a Prompt?</h2>
<p>
A prompt is the text or instruction you give to an AI model. It can be a question, command, or context description. The clearer the prompt, the better the AI’s response.
</p>

<h2>Principles of Effective Prompting</h2>
<ul>
<li>Be specific about the task or question</li>
<li>Provide context or background if needed</li>
<li>Use examples to clarify what you want</li>
<li>Break complex tasks into smaller prompts</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common Mistakes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Vague instructions that confuse the AI</li>
<li>Asking multiple unrelated questions in one prompt</li>
<li>Expecting exact answers without iteration</li>
</ul>

<h2>Tips for Beginners</h2>
<ul>
<li>Start simple and iterate gradually</li>
<li>Test different phrasings for better results</li>
<li>Include format or style instructions if needed</li>
</ul>

<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>
Mastering prompt engineering improves productivity and output quality when using AI models. With practice, you can get more accurate, relevant, and creative results.
</p>
